---
// Port of ../klub_biolocation/themes/void/layouts/_default/list.html, following the
// procedure in MIGRATION-PLAN.md §4.1. Class attributes are copied verbatim.
//
// This is a component rather than a page because Hugo uses the same list.html for two
// routes: /posts/ (the Posts menu item) and /categories/<slug>/. The only difference between
// them is the h1, so it is a prop. The tag pages look similar but are NOT this markup -
// taxonomy/tag.html differs in the year badge, the date cell and the tag chips, so it is
// ported separately in src/pages/tags/[slug]/[...page].astro. (Path changed 2026-09-19: the
// tag route moved there when the lists got pagination.)
//
// HOW THE GO TEMPLATE MAPS ONTO THIS FILE
//
//   .Title                       -> the `title` prop.
//   .Pages.GroupByDate "2006"    -> groupByYear() in lib/posts.ts. Years newest first.
//   .Key                         -> group.year.
//   .Pages.ByDate.Reverse        -> group.items, already newest first.
//   .RelPermalink                -> card.url: `/posts/<slug>/` from postCard() in
//                                   lib/posts.ts, `/video/<slug>/` from videoCard() in
//                                   lib/video.ts (since 2026-09-22).
//   .Date.Format (i18n "date_month_day_format")
//                                -> formatMonthDay(), i.e. Hugo's "Jan 02" layout.
//   .Summary | plainify | truncate 140
//                                -> card.summary: summary() in lib/summary.ts, applied by
//                                   postCard(); see its header for the one known divergence.
//   .Params.tags                 -> card.tags: post.data.tags, in front matter order,
//                                   lower-cased by the collection schema exactly as
//                                   hugo.toml's `tags = [":lower"]` rule does.
//   i18n "list_read_more"        -> card.action: t.list_read_more on a post,
//                                   t.list_watch_video on a video.
//
// DECISIONS WORTH KNOWING
//
// The card is covered by an absolutely positioned anchor (`absolute inset-0 z-10`) that
// carries the whole link, while the tag chips sit above it on `z-20` and stop the click from
// propagating. That is the theme's own construction and it is reproduced as-is.
//
// The tag chip hrefs had NO trailing slash until the evening of 2026-09-19, because Hugo
// builds them by hand as `{{ "/tags/" | relLangURL }}{{ . | urlize }}` and the live Hugo site
// links to `/tags/hugo`, not `/tags/hugo/`. The owner reported it as broken: with
// `trailingSlash: "always"` Astro's dev and preview servers answer such an address with 404
// (GitHub Pages redirects it, so nobody saw it live). The chips now link to `/tags/hugo/`, the
// address the page is built at; the same change was made to the chips of the tag route, its
// "All Tags" link and the category label in ArticleLayout.astro. REVIEW-FIXES.md, section 5.
//
// PAGINATION - changed 2026-09-19, asked for by the owner. This used to read "NOT PORTED":
// Hugo paginates at 10 posts and the site had two, so Hugo emitted no pagination markup and
// there was nothing to match. The owner has since asked for pages of 5 posts with Previous
// and Next links that move a whole page. What changed, and why:
//
//   .Paginator.HasPrev / .HasNext / .Prev.URL / .Next.URL
//                                -> page.prevUrl / page.nextUrl, from paginateList() in
//                                   lib/posts.ts, rendered by Pagination.astro since later
//                                   on 2026-09-19: list.html's block, classes verbatim, with
//                                   tag.html's SVG arrows in place of the text arrows.
//   i18n "pagination_previous" / "pagination_next"
//                                -> t.pagination_previous / t.pagination_next.
//
// - The prop is one page (`page`) instead of the whole list (`posts`), and the year groups are
//   built from `page.items`. Hugo's list.html ranges over `.Pages`, which is every post in the
//   section, not over `.Paginator.Pages`, the posts of the current page. So on the Hugo site
//   every page of a paginated list would show all the posts, and only the Previous and Next
//   links would change. That bug is not reproduced: here a page shows its own posts.
// - Every page holds one year, so it has exactly one year badge: the Posts list and, since the
//   evening of 2026-09-19, the category pages too are split by year (paginateByYear() in
//   lib/posts.ts). For a few hours that day the category pages were paginated across years,
//   and a year continuing from one page to the next got its badge again on the next page.
// - The year switcher under the h1 is new, asked for by the owner; Hugo has nothing like it.
//   Every route passes `years` and `currentYear` now, and the switcher renders only when there
//   are at least two years. Each link goes to the first page of its year under the list's own
//   address, and the year being shown is highlighted and carries aria-current. Its button
//   classes are the pagination buttons' classes from list.html, and the highlighted state uses
//   the year badge's colours, so it matches the theme in both colour schemes. Since later on
//   2026-09-19 it is YearSwitcher.astro, which also decides which years to show when there are
//   many, and ListByYear.astro places it and the page buttons around the list.
// See PAGINATION.md.
//
// CARDS - changed 2026-09-22 (VIDEO-PAGE.md, section 4). This file was PostList.astro and
// rendered posts. The Video list (/video/) renders through it as well now: the colleague's
// VideoList.astro was a copy of this file with the card's link changed, and it missed every
// fix the review brought here. The owner asked for posts and videos to stay apart, so the
// component knows neither: it renders Cards (lib/lists.ts), plain data the routes build with
// postCard() (lib/posts.ts) or videoCard() (lib/video.ts), and the only things that differ
// between a post and a video on a card - the address and the last line, "Read more" or the
// colleague's "Watch the video" - come inside the card. For a few hours that day the page held
// `Post | Video` entries and this file chose by the entry's collection.
import {
  groupByYear,
  type Card,
  type ListPage,
  type YearLink,
} from "../lib/lists";
import { formatMonthDay } from "../lib/date";
import { urlize, encodeSlug } from "../lib/urlize";
// Added later on 2026-09-19: the year switcher and the page buttons around the list, through
// one component shared with the tag route; see its header.
import ListByYear from "./ListByYear.astro";

interface Props {
  /** Hugo's `.Title`: "Posts" for the section, the term title for one category. */
  title: string;
  // Changed 2026-09-19: one page of the list instead of the whole list (`posts: Post[]`),
  // for pagination; see the note at the top. Cards since 2026-09-22 (was ListPage<Post>); see
  // CARDS above.
  page: ListPage<Card>;
  // Both required since the evening of 2026-09-19: every list is split by year, so every route
  // passes them (they were optional while only /posts/ had the switcher).
  /** Every year of the list, newest first, for the year switcher. */
  years: YearLink[];
  /** The year the page shows, highlighted in the year switcher; undefined on an empty list. */
  currentYear: string | undefined;
}

const { title, page, years, currentYear } = Astro.props;
const groups = groupByYear(page.items);
---

<div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-8">
  <h1 class="mb-8 text-center text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800">{title}</h1>

  {
    /* Added 2026-09-19: the year switcher above the list and the page buttons below it; see
    the note at the top. First inline here, then YearSwitcher.astro and Pagination.astro, and
    since the evening ListByYear.astro, which places both around the list the same way on
    every list route. The switcher's label stays a literal because the theme's strings, ported
    in full to src/i18n/strings.ts, have no key for it. */
  }
  <ListByYear page={page} years={years} currentYear={currentYear}>
    <div class="space-y-16">
      {
        groups.map((group) => (
          <div class="relative">
            {/* Year indicator */}
            <div class="mb-6 flex items-center">
              <div class="year-indicator-badge flex h-16 w-16 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-50 to-blue-100 text-xl font-bold text-blue-700 shadow-sm dark:from-slate-700/40 dark:to-slate-800/40 dark:text-blue-300">
                {group.year}
              </div>
              <div class="ml-4 h-px flex-grow bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-200 to-transparent dark:from-slate-600" />
            </div>

            {/* Article list. The theme's `ml-8` became `sm:ml-8` on 2026-09-19 evening
            (REVIEW-FIXES.md, section 9): the 2rem timeline indent under the year badge put the
            cards 80px from the left edge of a phone and 48px from the right, which the reviewer
            read as "shifted right". Below 640px the cards now span the column; from 640px up
            the class is what it was, so nothing changes on a laptop. Hugo renders the indent at
            every width. */}
            <div class="space-y-6 sm:ml-8">
              {group.items.map((card) => (
                <div class="relative">
                  {/* card.url since 2026-09-22, was `/posts/${post.slug}/`; see CARDS above. */}
                  <a
                    href={card.url}
                    class="absolute inset-0 z-10"
                    aria-label={card.title}
                  />
                  <div class="group overflow-hidden rounded-lg bg-white shadow-sm transition-shadow duration-300 hover:shadow-md dark:bg-slate-900">
                    <div class="p-5">
                      <div class="mb-3 flex flex-col justify-between sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline">
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-gray-800 transition-colors group-hover:text-blue-600 dark:text-gray-100">
                          {card.title}
                        </h3>
                        <time class="mt-1 flex flex-shrink-0 items-center text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 sm:ml-4 sm:mt-0">
                          <svg
                            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                            class="mr-1 h-4 w-4 text-gray-400"
                            fill="none"
                            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                            stroke="currentColor"
                          >
                            <path
                              stroke-linecap="round"
                              stroke-linejoin="round"
                              stroke-width="2"
                              d="M8 7V3m8 4V3m-9 8h10M5 21h14a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2z"
                            />
                          </svg>
                          {formatMonthDay(card.date)}
                        </time>
                      </div>

                      {card.summary && (
                        <div class="line-clamp-2 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
                          {card.summary}
                        </div>
                      )}

                      {card.tags.length > 0 && (
                        <div class="relative z-20 mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                          {/* Changed 2026-09-19: the parameter was annotated `any`, which the
                          house rules forbid and which nothing needed - the collection schema
                          declares `tags` as string[], so `tag` is inferred as string, as in the
                          tag route's copy of these chips. */}
                          {card.tags.map((tag) => (
                            <a
                              href={`/tags/${encodeSlug(urlize(tag))}/`}
                              class="tag-chip rounded bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 text-xs text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-gray-300 dark:hover:bg-slate-700"
                              onclick="event.stopPropagation();"
                            >
                              {tag}
                            </a>
                          ))}
                        </div>
                      )}

                      <div class="mt-4">
                        <span class="inline-flex items-center text-sm text-blue-600 transition-transform duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-1">
                          {/* card.action since 2026-09-22: "Read more" on a post, "Watch the
                          video" on a video; see CARDS above. */}
                          {card.action}
                          <svg
                            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                            class="ml-1 h-4 w-4"
                            fill="none"
                            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                            stroke="currentColor"
                          >
                            <path
                              stroke-linecap="round"
                              stroke-linejoin="round"
                              stroke-width="2"
                              d="M14 5l7 7m0 0l-7 7m7-7H3"
                            />
                          </svg>
                        </span>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </ListByYear>
</div>
